  "question": {
    "html": "<p>An object of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.10\\ \\text{kg}\"></span> performs simple harmonic motion according to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x(t) = 0.060 \\sin(20t)\"></span> (in metres and seconds).</p><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> Determine the speed of the object when the displacement is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x = 0.040\\ \\text{m}\"></span>. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> Calculate the total mechanical energy of the object. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c\"><p><strong>c</strong> Determine the time it takes for the object to move from <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x = 0.040\\ \\text{m}\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x = 0\"></span>. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"d\"><p><strong>d</strong> Calculate the acceleration of the object when <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x = 0.040\\ \\text{m}\"></span>. [1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"e\"><p><strong>e</strong> Sketch an energy vs. displacement graph, indicating both kinetic and potential energy variations. [2]</p></section>"
